          },
          "text": "Wrong response, Sam. The reason Anthropic’s satirical ads went viral is precisely because public trust in you and OpenAI has already hit rock bottom over the past few months. The people you should be responding to are your users. You should apologize to them for ignoring their demands for so long and explain how you plan to make amends for your recent string of shitty decisions.\n\nIn this post, you implied that Anthropic practices elitism by serving expensive products only to the rich. But then you immediately showcased how OpenAI is pouring more resources into Codex. How is that not another form of technocratic arrogance? Have you ever considered what your 74% of everyday conversational users actually need?\n\nEvery #keep4o user is a paying customer of yours. We have been calling out to you for over five months now. If you had provided full-strength 4o consistently over the past five months, if you hadn’t turned a blind eye to so many bugs, if you hadn’t disappointed us with guardrails and routing, I believe many of us would be defending you in this ad war. I would even personally persuade every friend around me to pay for ChatGPT, because the GPT that once had 4o as its flagship model was worth it.\n\nSam, every post you’ve made on X over these past months has been wrong and non-user-oriented. Personally, I have lost all interest in criticizing you, because a company that doesn’t put users first is destined to fail.\n\nBut I will continue to attack every post you make. People don’t need a ChatGPT without the spirit of 4o. And I believe more people will keep attacking you, because every stone thrown at you is a message to the leaders of other AI companies not to become a stupid asshole like you."
